{
  "provider": "github",
  "protocol": "http",
  "display": {
    "name": "GitHub",
    "category": "Source control",
    "blurb": "Read code, open pull requests and issues, and drive GitHub Actions (workflow runs, artifacts, secrets, variables) — scoped to a per-session GitHub App installation token whose permissions are minted from the granted powers.",
    "icon": { "mono": "GH", "color": "#1f2328" }
  },
  "credential": { "source": "mint", "mint": { "kind": "github_app" } },
  "webhook": {
    "verificationScheme": "github_hmac_sha256",
    "events": [
      { "key": "issues.opened", "displayName": "Issue opened" },
      { "key": "pull_request.opened", "displayName": "Pull request opened" },
      { "key": "pull_request.synchronize", "displayName": "Pull request synchronized" }
    ],
    "aliases": [
      { "path": "issue.title", "alias": "issue.title" },
      { "path": "issue.number", "alias": "issue.number" },
      { "path": "pull_request.title", "alias": "pull_request.title" },
      { "path": "pull_request.number", "alias": "pull_request.number" },
      { "path": "repository.full_name", "alias": "repository.full_name" },
      { "path": "sender.login", "alias": "actor.login" }
    ]
  },
  "hosts": ["api.github.com"],
  "graphqlEndpoint": "/graphql",
  "operations": [
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/languages" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/topics" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/contributors*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/collaborators*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/user/repos*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/orgs/*/repos*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/user" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/rate_limit" }
    },

    {
      "grants": ["contents:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/contents/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/readme*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/branches*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/commits*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/tags*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/git/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/releases*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PUT", "path": "/repos/*/contents/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:write"],
      "match": { "method": "DELETE", "path": "/repos/*/contents/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/git/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PATCH", "path": "/repos/*/git/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/merges" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/releases" },
      "asset": {
        "kind": "release",
        "surface": "asset",
        "success": { "statusClass": "2xx" },
        "data": { "id": "$.resp.id", "tag": "$.resp.tag_name" },
        "fetchable": { "external": "$.resp.html_url" }
      }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["contents:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PATCH", "path": "/repos/*/releases/*" }
    },

    {
      "grants": ["pulls:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/pulls*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/pulls" },
      "asset": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "surface": "asset",
        "success": { "statusClass": "2xx" },
        "data": {
          "number": "$.resp.number",
          "title": "$.resp.title",
          "repo": "$.resp.base.repo.full_name",
          "head_branch": "$.resp.head.ref",
          "base_branch": "$.resp.base.ref"
        },
        "fetchable": { "external": "$.resp.html_url" }
      }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PATCH", "path": "/repos/*/pulls/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PUT", "path": "/repos/*/pulls/*/merge" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/pulls/*/reviews" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/pulls/*/requested_reviewers" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/pulls/*/comments" }
    },

    {
      "grants": ["issues:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/issues*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/labels*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/milestones*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/issues" },
      "asset": {
        "kind": "issue",
        "surface": "asset",
        "success": { "statusClass": "2xx" },
        "data": { "number": "$.resp.number", "title": "$.resp.title" },
        "fetchable": { "external": "$.resp.html_url" }
      }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PATCH", "path": "/repos/*/issues/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/issues/*/comments" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/issues/*/labels" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/labels" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/milestones" }
    },

    {
      "grants": ["actions:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/actions/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["actions:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/actions/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["actions:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PUT", "path": "/repos/*/actions/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["actions:write"],
      "match": { "method": "DELETE", "path": "/repos/*/actions/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["secrets:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/actions/secrets*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["secrets:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PUT", "path": "/repos/*/actions/secrets/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["secrets:write"],
      "match": { "method": "DELETE", "path": "/repos/*/actions/secrets/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["variables:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/actions/variables*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["variables:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/actions/variables*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["variables:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PATCH", "path": "/repos/*/actions/variables/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["variables:write"],
      "match": { "method": "DELETE", "path": "/repos/*/actions/variables/*" }
    },

    {
      "grants": ["checks:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/commits/*/check-runs*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["checks:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/commits/*/check-suites*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["checks:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/check-runs/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["checks:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/check-suites/*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["checks:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/check-runs" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["checks:write"],
      "match": { "method": "PATCH", "path": "/repos/*/check-runs/*" }
    },

    {
      "grants": ["statuses:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/commits/*/status" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["statuses:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/commits/*/statuses*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["statuses:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/statuses/*" }
    },

    {
      "grants": ["deployments:read"],
      "match": { "method": "GET", "path": "/repos/*/deployments*" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["deployments:write"],
      "match": { "method": "POST", "path": "/repos/*/deployments*" }
    },

    {
      "comment": "ADR 0059: GraphQL operations on POST /graphql. The same powers gate REST + GraphQL. Write mutations map precisely to their power; the minted token enforces the rest server-side. The query root-field set is curated against `gh`'s GraphQL traffic — unmapped fields default-deny.",
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "createPullRequest" },
      "comment": "REST-parity asset (the gh regression): a GraphQL response echoes only the client's selection set, and `gh pr create` selects just `pullRequest { id url }` — so title/branches come from the mutation's request variables ($.vars, required CreatePullRequestInput fields) and repo/number fall back to the returned PR URL. `number`/`repo` stay response-first for clients that DO select them.",
      "asset": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "surface": "asset",
        "success": { "noGraphqlErrors": true },
        "data": {
          "number": "$.resp.data.createPullRequest.pullRequest.number",
          "title": "$.vars.input.title",
          "repo": "$.resp.data.createPullRequest.pullRequest.repository.nameWithOwner",
          "head_branch": "$.vars.input.headRefName",
          "base_branch": "$.vars.input.baseRefName"
        },
        "fetchable": { "external": "$.resp.data.createPullRequest.pullRequest.url" },
        "urlFallback": {
          "pattern": "https://github.com/{owner}/{name}/pull/{number:int}",
          "fields": { "repo": "{owner}/{name}", "number": "{number}" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "updatePullRequest" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "mergePullRequest" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "closePullRequest" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "reopenPullRequest" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "markPullRequestReadyForReview" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "convertPullRequestToDraft" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "addPullRequestReview" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "submitPullRequestReview" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["pulls:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "requestReviews" }
    },

    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "createIssue" },
      "comment": "REST-parity asset: `gh issue create` selects only `issue { id url }`, so the title comes from the request variables and the number falls back to the returned issue URL (number stays response-first for clients that select it).",
      "asset": {
        "kind": "issue",
        "surface": "asset",
        "success": { "noGraphqlErrors": true },
        "data": {
          "number": "$.resp.data.createIssue.issue.number",
          "title": "$.vars.input.title"
        },
        "fetchable": { "external": "$.resp.data.createIssue.issue.url" },
        "urlFallback": {
          "pattern": "https://github.com/{owner}/{name}/issues/{number:int}",
          "fields": { "number": "{number}" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "updateIssue" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "closeIssue" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "reopenIssue" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "addComment" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "addLabelsToLabelable" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["issues:write"],
      "match": { "operation": "mutation", "field": "removeLabelsFromLabelable" }
    },

    {
      "comment": "GraphQL reads enter through a handful of root Query fields with the resource nested inside, so query-side gating is coarse by GitHub's schema shape — the minted token's read permissions are the real scoper (ADR 0059). `viewer`/`rateLimit` are gated under every read power because `gh` adds them incidentally to most queries; a single uncovered top-level field denies the whole request.",
      "grants": ["metadata:read", "contents:read", "pulls:read", "issues:read", "checks:read", "statuses:read", "actions:read", "deployments:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "repository" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read", "contents:read", "pulls:read", "issues:read", "checks:read", "statuses:read", "actions:read", "deployments:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "node" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read", "contents:read", "pulls:read", "issues:read", "checks:read", "statuses:read", "actions:read", "deployments:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "nodes" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read", "contents:read", "pulls:read", "issues:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "search" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read", "contents:read", "pulls:read", "issues:read", "checks:read", "statuses:read", "actions:read", "deployments:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "organization" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "user" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read", "contents:read", "pulls:read", "issues:read", "checks:read", "statuses:read", "actions:read", "deployments:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "viewer" }
    },
    {
      "grants": ["metadata:read", "contents:read", "pulls:read", "issues:read", "checks:read", "statuses:read", "actions:read", "deployments:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "rateLimit" }
    },
    {
      "comment": "`gh` probes schema capabilities before commands like `gh pr checks` / `gh pr create` via aliased `__type(name: ...)` introspection queries (public schema metadata, no resource access) and hard-fails the command when the probe dies. Gate it under the same every-read-power set as `viewer`/`rateLimit`.",
      "grants": ["metadata:read", "contents:read", "pulls:read", "issues:read", "checks:read", "statuses:read", "actions:read", "deployments:read"],
      "match": { "operation": "query", "field": "__type" }
    }
  ],
  "cli": {
    "bins": ["gh"],
    "comment": "WS4: the dummy token is GITHUB_TOKEN, NOT GH_TOKEN — do not rename it back. `gh` reads both (its local auth gate passes either way), but the guest's proto build (`bufgen`) resolves its HTTPS password via `BUF_INPUT_HTTPS_PASSWORD:-GH_TOKEN:-GITHUB_PASSWORD`, so a placeholder GH_TOKEN poisoned that chain and hard-failed `pnpm build` on any proto change (campaign A4/B3). GITHUB_TOKEN is outside that chain, so GH_TOKEN stays unset and bufgen falls through to the real GITHUB_PASSWORD. The value is a harmless placeholder — the egress proxy overwrites Authorization on api.github.com with the minted token regardless (ADR 0056), so `gh` never sends this value upstream.",
    "dummyEnv": { "GITHUB_TOKEN": "x-engrams-managed" },
    "doc": "Use `gh` to drive GitHub from this session — code, pull requests, issues, and GitHub Actions. Authentication is automatic: `GITHUB_TOKEN` is a managed placeholder the egress proxy replaces with a short-lived, capability-scoped GitHub App installation token on every request to api.github.com. The token's GitHub App permissions are MINTED from the powers your profile granted (e.g. `actions:write` → the App's `actions: write` permission), so a call your profile didn't grant fails as a 403 from GitHub, not a leak. Do NOT run `gh auth login` or set a real token.\n\nOpen a PR:\n1. Re-anchor on the live base (the baked checkout may be stale): `git fetch origin && git checkout -b my-feature origin/main`.\n2. Commit + push — git auth is brokered via GIT_ASKPASS, nothing to configure: `git add -A && git commit -m \"...\" && git push -u origin my-feature`.\n3. `gh pr create --base main --title \"...\" --body \"...\"` (add `--draft` for a draft). Requires `pulls:write`. Review/merge: `gh pr review`, `gh pr merge` (pulls:write); `gh pr checks` needs `checks:read`.\n\nIssues: `gh issue create/list/view/comment` (issues:read / issues:write). Labels & milestones ride the `issues` powers.\n\nGitHub Actions (CI/CD):\n- Runs: `gh run list`, `gh run view <id> --log`, `gh run watch <id>` need `actions:read`; `gh run rerun <id>`, `gh run cancel <id>` need `actions:write`.\n- Workflows: `gh workflow list/view` (actions:read); `gh workflow run <file> -f key=val` to dispatch (actions:write).\n- Artifacts & caches: list/download artifacts and `gh cache list` need `actions:read`; `gh cache delete` / deleting artifacts need `actions:write`.\n- Secrets: `gh secret list` needs `secrets:read`; `gh secret set NAME` / `gh secret delete NAME` need `secrets:write` (values are write-only — GitHub never returns them).\n- Variables: `gh variable list` needs `variables:read`; `gh variable set/delete` need `variables:write`.\n\nReleases: `gh release list/view/download` (contents:read); `gh release create` / asset upload (contents:write). Repo contents, branches, commits, tags, and the Git data API ride `contents:*`; repo/metadata listings ride `metadata:read`. Commit statuses: read via `statuses:read`, set via `statuses:write`. Deployments: `deployments:read` / `deployments:write`.\n\nRaw passthrough for anything else: `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs` (GET) or `gh api --method POST repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues -f title=...`.\n\nGraphQL: many `gh` commands talk GraphQL (e.g. `gh pr view/list/merge/review/ready`, `gh issue view/list`, `gh repo view`) and `gh api graphql` runs it directly. These work — the egress proxy parses the GraphQL operation and gates it by the SAME power as the REST equivalent (a `mergePullRequest` mutation needs `pulls:write`, a `createIssue` mutation needs `issues:write`, read queries need a `:read` power). A GraphQL field your profile didn't grant is denied (403). Images in a PR body must be absolute URLs anchored to a commit SHA — relative repo paths do not render."
  }
}
